abstract: >-
  A geometric approach to the 3D incompressible Navier–Stokes global-regularity
  problem on the periodic torus, with a Lean 4 formalization. The work introduces
  a symplectic "tether" construction on coadjoint orbits and a two-layer
  geometric/analytic architecture. This is a priority-preserving formalization
  artifact with documented schematic holes; it does not claim a completed,
  kernel-closed solution of the Clay Navier–Stokes Millennium Problem.
